The default local decision-router model, convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions
(https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions), is licensed
Apache-2.0 and is not bundled with this repository; `scripts/setup-laya.ps1`
downloads it separately from Hugging Face at install time, pinned to a
validated revision. It is built on the ModernBERT-large encoder by Answer.AI
and LightOn. An alternative checkpoint, Luni/laya-grounded
(https://huggingface.co/Luni/laya-grounded), can be installed instead by
passing `-Repo` to `scripts/setup-laya.ps1`; it is licensed CC-BY-NC-4.0
(non-commercial), so anyone building a commercial product on top of POK-Agent
must not select it and should keep the Apache-2.0 default (see
`docs/decision-router-backends.md`).

The optional local cross-model judge, php-ai/zeiger-0.6b
(https://huggingface.co/php-ai/zeiger-0.6b), is licensed CC-BY-SA-4.0 (weights)
and is disabled by default. It is not bundled with this repository;
`scripts/setup-zeiger.ps1` downloads it separately from Hugging Face at
install time, pinned to a validated revision. CC-BY-SA-4.0 requires that
adaptations of the weights themselves (not POK-Agent's own source code, which
this NOTICE does not extend to) be shared under the same license if
redistributed; downloading and running the checkpoint locally does not
require anything of POK-Agent's own Apache-2.0 codebase.

Voice input uses sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx,
Apache-2.0), linked as a library. Its speech models are not bundled with this
repository; the app downloads them from the sherpa-onnx releases when the user
installs voice input:

- sherpa-onnx-streaming-zipformer-en-2023-06-26 (k2-fsa, Apache-2.0), used for
  live captions.
- NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3),
  licensed CC-BY-4.0, in its sherpa-onnx int8 export, used for the final text.
  Attribution: "Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3" by NVIDIA, CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); converted to ONNX and
  quantized by the sherpa-onnx project.
- Silero VAD (https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad, MIT), used to find
  phrases in multilingual mode.
